  topic="buying property from an NRI"
  lead="If you buy property from a non-resident seller, you must deduct TDS under section 393(2), not the 1 percent that applies to a resident seller. The tax is charged at the rate for the seller's capital gain, plus surcharge and cess, and unless the seller holds a lower deduction certificate it is usually deducted on the full sale consideration. From 1 October 2026, a resident individual or HUF buyer files Form 141, Schedule E, without a TAN."
